# Harden the parser against <script> tags & "quoted" input

**Stack:** Rust 1.98, serde & serde_yaml

## Context

Refer to these files for background:

- `./docs/a<b>.md`

## Instructions

- When working in `src/**/*.rs`: Reject input containing `<` or `&` unless it is escaped **(REQUIRED)**
- Keep `Record<T>` generics intact in error messages **(REQUIRED)**
- Prefer `&str` over `String` in the "hot" paths *(preferred)*
- Changing the <envelope> tag vocabulary **(ASK FIRST)**

## Protected Files

- `src/**/*.rs`: Every Rust source file, including "generated" ones
- `docs/a&b/**`: Ampersand in a path

## Assumptions

- [ ] Input can carry a fenced code block with markup
- [x] Both `'` and `"` survive the round-trip

## Deliverable

Well-formed XML whose text keeps A & B < C > D and 'single' and "double" quotes intact.

## Notes

A fenced block with markup in it:

```rust
fn main() {
    if a < b && c > d {
        println!("{}", "<tag attr='v'>");
    }
}
```
